    "readme_description": "The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance\" target=\"_blank\">Hamming distance</a> between two integers is the number of positions at which the corresponding bits are different.\n\nGiven an integer array <code>nums</code>, return <em>the sum of <strong>Hamming distances</strong> between all the pairs of the integers in</em> <code>nums</code>.",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: nums = [4,14,2]\nOutput: 6\nExplanation: In binary representation, the 4 is 0100, 14 is 1110, and 2 is 0010 (just\nshowing the four bits relevant in this case).\nThe answer will be:\nHammingDistance(4, 14) + HammingDistance(4, 2) + HammingDistance(14, 2) = 2 + 2 + 2 = 6.\n```"
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: nums = [4,14,4]\nOutput: 4\n```"
            }
        ]
    },
